    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass (3/3, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\nI implemented address normalization in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the only owner-creation endpoint):\n\n- **New `normalizeAddress` method** \u2014 trims and collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, then expands street-type abbreviations token-by-token (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). A `null`/whitespace-only value normalizes to `\"\"`.\n- **Required-field check** now runs against the normalized address, so an address that is blank after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"`) is rejected with 400.\n- **Storage/response** \u2014 the normalized value is written back onto the DTO before mapping, so it is stored and returned (`\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`).\n- **Address comparisons** \u2014 household duplicate detection and the shared household id now both use the normalized address form; `normalizeHousehold` remains for the last-name comparison and its javadoc was narrowed accordingly.\n\nThe V2 controller only lists owners, so no change was needed there.",
